Do not turn every rustc warning into a hard error.

"warnings = deny" is a useful policy for upstream CI, which pins its own
toolchain, but it makes the package fail to build the moment the distribution
rustc (which moves independently of upstream's rust-version floor) grows a new
lint. The unsafe_code deny is kept -- that one is a deliberate design
constraint, not a lint-drift hazard.

Index: rtk-0.47.0/Cargo.toml
===================================================================
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -80,4 +80,3 @@
 
 [lints.rust]
 unsafe_code = "deny"
-warnings = "deny"
